  "output_text": "{\"issues\":[],\"reason\":\"The proof is correct. It uses that m=(p-1)/2 is odd, proves in the forward direction that (-a)^m≡1 and every exponent annihilating -a is divisible by m, and in the converse proves that every exponent annihilating a is divisible by 2m while a^(2m)≡1. Thus the claimed orders follow exactly.\"}",
